     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "What advantages does the ZOLLER »micBox« offer compared to manual mounting of cutterheads?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The fully automated processes, which run independently of the operating personnel, guarantee maximum process reliability. An additional, invaluable advantage is the end-to-end traceability. Furthermore, the continuous production operation enables a significant increase in efficiency as well as considerable cost savings - decisive economic advantages for the future.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c2511",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How can the indexable inserts be changed in the »micBox«?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The software and the database function with the associated tool ID document how often an insert or screw has been used for each tool.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c2509",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Up to which tool holder sizes can tools be accommodated in a »micBox«?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>With the ZOLLER spindle, the »micBox« can accommodate tools up to HSK 125.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c2507",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Is the screwdriving unit additionally monitored and can the torque be variably adjusted in a »micBox«?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The screwdriving unit mounted on the robot monitors the torque each time the screw is tightened. Depending on the screw, cutter head and indexable insert, this can be set up to 7 Nm (maximum 10 Nm).</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c2505",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
